  "story": "The Netherlands consumer price index (CPI) has shown an upward trend since 2019, with the overall index reaching 105.13 in October 2026 compared to the base year 2025=100. Food prices have increased from 94.61 in January 2024 to 99.1 in October 2026, while energy prices rose from 95.22 to 99.1 over the same period. Housing costs, represented by both actual rent and imputed rent for owner-occupied homes, have seen the most significant increases, rising from 92.59 to 106.91 over this period."
